sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser
    participant R as Flask request thread
    participant Q as queue.Queue
    participant D as Daemon thread

    B->>R: POST /api/query
    Note over B,R: 400 on a blank query or an<br/>unknown provider — the only<br/>HTTP error status in the flow
    R->>Q: create_session(uuid4())
    Note over R,Q: an UNBOUNDED in-memory queue<br/>in _sessions, plus the 21-key<br/>initial_state with session_id

    par producer — the pipeline
        R->>D: Thread(target=_run, daemon=True).start()
        D->>Q: emit(session_id, type, data)
        Note over Q,D: emit() → q.put, from 31 call sites.<br/>A NO-OP for an unknown session — make<br/>it raise and a dead browser crashes<br/>the whole pipeline.
    and consumer — the SSE generator
        R-->>B: 200 text/event-stream
        Note over B,R: the headers are now committed —<br/>every later failure is in-band
        alt an item arrives within 180 s
            Q->>R: q.get(timeout=180)
            R-->>B: data: {json}
            Note over B,R: the timeout is PER EVENT —<br/>the clock resets on every frame
        else queue.Empty
            R-->>B: data: error — Stream timeout
            R->>Q: close_session() — pops the queue
            Note over Q,D: Frees the SOCKET, never the COMPUTE.<br/>The daemon runs to completion, and<br/>every later emit() no-ops into an<br/>orphaned queue.
        end
    end

    D->>Q: put done — bypasses emit()
    D->>Q: finally: put(None) — sentinel
    Q->>R: None
    R-->>B: data: stream_end
    R->>Q: close_session() — pops the queue
    Note over B,D: done · error · stream_end are ROUTE-framed, not node-emitted.<br/>close_session() pushes a 2nd sentinel that nobody reads.
